Sat Oct  3 15:17:13 UTC 2026 - Martin Pluskal <mpluskal@suse.com>

- Update to 0.5.14, which also carries 0.5.13 (opencode v2 pins
  @opentui/* at exactly this version; the FFI ABI is private and
  unversioned, so both halves and every consumer move together):
  * Fixed a leak in the native text buffer: replacing a buffer's
    contents kept the whole previous rope alive, so a 2000-line
    text grew RSS by 1.24 MB per call and 2000 calls reached
    2.5 GB. Bytes loaded from a file no longer sit in the rope
    arena where the next document could pick them up either
  * Fixed the terminal not repainting when a debounced SIGWINCH
    burst shrank and restored the original geometry inside the
    100 ms window, which could leave a stale screen until some
    later resize
  * Fixed a busy rerender loop: a child attached after a layout
    pass makes Yoga report NaN dimensions, and since NaN is never
    equal to itself the layout kept being redone
  * Fixed the SolidJS portal leaking its children's listeners on
    teardown
  * Under tmux, terminal capability probes are now sent unwrapped,
    so tmux answers the pane that asked instead of a pane switch
    delivering the reply to the wrong pane as input. Focus tracking
    is enabled whenever tmux is detected, and an explicitly
    requested Sixel protocol is honoured through passthrough
  * Fixed kitty graphics drawn above the cell background
  * Cut FFI traffic and per-cell work in the native core: selection
    updates skip the native reset for text views with no selection,
    buffer resizes reallocate only once the cells stop fitting (and
    a failed resize now leaves the buffer unchanged instead of
    shortening a cell array), and colour bytes round without a libm
    call
  * Draw text and box titles encode into reused storage rather than
    allocating a buffer per call
  * Many more fixes and improvements; see upstream's release notes
    for the full list

-------------------------------------------------------------------
Sun Sep 27 15:46:57 UTC 2026 - Martin Pluskal <mpluskal@suse.com>

- Update to 0.5.12 (opencode v2 pins @opentui/* at exactly this
  version; the FFI ABI is unversioned so both move together):
  * Native core now needs Zig 0.16 and lives in packages/native;
    its Zig dependencies and image libraries ship vendored in-tree
  * New embedded terminal runtime and native image rendering in
    the library, plus audio input capture and clipboard support
  * Per-line text alignment, mouse pointer styles, double/triple
    click and CJK line wrapping in the TypeScript API
  * Renderer and input fixes: split-footer resize, transparent
    terminal backgrounds, markdown tables and hyperlinks, Thai
    spacing marks and Ghostty wide grapheme widths
  * Many more fixes and improvements; see upstream's release notes
    for the full list
- Drop opentui-build-id.patch (upstream sets the build ID itself)
  and rework opentui-baseline-cpu.patch for the moved build.zig
- Retire opentui-zig-deps-0.4.5.tar.zst and opentui_zigdeps: deps
  are vendored in-tree, unpacked at build time, nothing is fetched
- Licence now Apache-2.0 AND BSD-3-Clause AND MIT AND
  (Unlicense OR MIT-0) for the vendored wuffs and libwebp code
- Skip two X11 clipboard unit tests on aarch64, where they abort
  the test runner (opentui-aarch64-skip-crashing-x11-tests.patch);
  create /tmp/.X11-unix in %check for the socket bind test

